# `create-astroid/template/` is NOT source — it is the scaffold's template set.
#
# Its files carry `__ASTROID_*__` placeholders that index.mjs substitutes at
# scaffold time, and several are deliberately not valid TypeScript on their own.
# The sharpest case:
#
#     MAIL_FROM: string;__ASTROID_ENV_BINDINGS__
#
# The placeholder sits on the same line with no terminator, because the value
# substituted in starts with a newline and every line it emits already ends in
# `;`. Format that and oxfmt splits the line and adds the "missing" semicolon,
# which expands to `SQUARE_ENVIRONMENT: string;;` in every scaffolded project —
# `astro check` then fails with TS1131 on a brand-new install.
#
# Nothing in this repo type-checks the template until it is scaffolded, so the
# clean-room smoke test is the only thing that catches it. Leave it alone.
packages/create-astroid/template/
